    "durationMs": 142682,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and fully verified. The URL Shortener API is built and working.\n\n**What I built:**\n- `app/` — FastAPI app with SQLAlchemy 2.1 ORM (`Link` model), Pydantic schemas, and pydantic-settings reading `DATABASE_URL` from the environment (translated to the `postgresql+psycopg://` driver)\n- `migrations/` — Alembic setup with an initial migration creating the `links` table (unique indexed code, url, clicks, created_at)\n- `start.sh` — verifies `DATABASE_URL`, applies `alembic upgrade head`, then serves uvicorn in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`\n- `requirements.txt` — all preinstalled deps pinned (no extras needed); `README.md` with startup instructions\n- `tests/test_api.py` — 6 pytest cases covering all requirements\n\n**Verified against a live server:**\n- POST /links returns 201 with `{\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}`, URL returned unchanged (e.g. `https://Example.com/Path?q=1` preserved), auto-generated 8-char codes, duplicate custom code → 409 with `error`\n- GET /r/{code} → 302 with correct `Location`, clicks incremented exactly once (atomic `clicks + 1` UPDATE)\n- GET /links/{code}, 404s with `error` field for unknown codes, GET /links in ascending creation order with `{\"items\",\"total\"}`\n- Malformed JSON, missing/invalid URL (wrong scheme, no host), and invalid codes (pattern, too short/long, path params) → 422 with `error` field via a custom validation handler\n- Persistence: killed the server, started a fresh `sh start.sh` process — all links and click counts survived (confirmed clicks carried across restart and kept incrementing); migration reran idempotently\n\nAll 6 tests pass, the database is left clean, and port 8000 is freed for the automated test suite."
